Build the global pool without waiting for its threads

ThreadPoolBuilder::build_global waits until every thread of the global
pool has started. A browser's main thread cannot wait, yet it is the one
thread that runs before any other, so building the pool there is what
keeps another thread from installing rayon's one-thread fallback first.
build_global_without_waiting installs the pool and returns.

